  "body": "## What changed\n\nA still frame with chains in the open operation's selection took 0.4-1.6 s. Each frame did three costly things again:\n\n- `model::features_of` content-hashed all the facets of the model.\n- `feature::resolve_chain` walked all the model's chains (about 5 ms) for each chain and for each caller (chips, stitch, account, region, refusal, overlay).\n- `pocket_region_on_part` sliced the part at each ladder plane (about 15 ms), for each of three `region_of` calls.\n\nThis PR adds three caches of derived values and one per-scene memo. No cache is a command. No cache is in the project file. Each key is the input itself, so a stale answer cannot occur:\n\n1. `model::features_of_shared` (app): the features of one model, keyed by the allocation of its facet `Arc`. A landing (`set_facets`) makes a new allocation, thus a new key.\n2. `model::resolve_chain` (app, new `model/chain_memo.rs`): the chain for one `ChainId`, keyed by the allocation of the `Arc<Features>`.\n3. `operation::pocket_memo` (app, new file): the pocket family's region on a part, keyed by the exact input (loops, part facets, planes, unit). The region and the `Invalid` / `Empty` refusals are kept.\n4. `frame_memo::scene_scope` (ui, new file): one `region_of` for each operation in one `world::collect`. The memo is dropped at the end of the scope.\n\nThe change of `feature::resolve_chain(` to `model::resolve_chain(` in about 15 files is a signature ripple, not new logic. The pick result, the stitch result and all cut geometry are the same. The hover path and the highlighter (#2201) are not changed.\n\nDecision file: `docs/decisions/2235-selection-frame-cost.md` (it quotes the maintainer).\n\n## Readings (headless, release, fig8.step, 8-10 chains on the top edge)\n\n| Stage | Scene collect | UI step |\n|---|---|---|\n| Before | 640-765 ms | 425-510 ms |\n| After the features and chain memos | 48-50 ms | 18-19 ms |\n| After the pocket memo | 9.5 ms | 6 ms |\n| After the per-scene memo | 5.8-6.4 ms | 5.1-5.7 ms |\n\nOne real frame is about 6 ms headless. Of that, `region_of` is about 1.6 ms (the ladder's facet copies in `material_of`). The rest is egui layout and the overlay. A still frame makes no feature digest, no chain walk and no part slice.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::tests::selection_frame_cost::frames_without_a_change_walk_digest_and_slice_nothing` (ui): 10 still frames add no chain walk, digest or slice, and exactly one region build per scene.\n- `egui_app::tests::selection_frame_cost::a_selection_change_or_a_landing_is_a_new_answer` (ui): a new selection walks and slices again and the region follows it; a landing takes a new digest and walk; the drawn region equals the fresh compute.\n- `operation::pocket_memo::law::a_hit_is_the_fresh_answer_and_any_changed_input_slices_again` (app lib)\n- `model::chain_memo::tests::a_hit_answers_what_a_fresh_walk_answers_and_walks_once` (app lib)\n\n## Gate\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick` selects all suites, because origin/main is 36 commits ahead of the branch base. So I ran the touched binaries instead:\n\n- `camcraft-app --lib` (354 pass) and 35 app test binaries: area_chains, area_picks, area_open, area_controls, pocket_recognition, rest_pocket, whole_model_pocket, pocket_overhead, slot_picks, slot_pick_refusals, feature, feature_pick, pick, pick_doors, heights_selection, stitch_cross, probe_pick, golden_cl, posting, recorded_post_streams, solid_law_goldens, opframe_picks, box_pick, circle_centre, circular_pick, centre_pick, contour_open_side, contour_auto_level, mcp_pick, mcp_pockets, commands_undo, wire_contour, align_axes, points_align, plane_align_edges. All pass.\n- `camcraft-ui` full suite (lib 956 pass, 6 ignored, and all ui test binaries). All pass.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nGoldens (`golden_cl`, `solid_law_goldens`, `recorded_post_streams`, `posting`) did not move.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GPU frame time in the real app. The readings are headless. A release test build is for the maintainer.\n- The hover path (#2201) is not measured or changed.\n- The heavy release lanes and the pixel snapshots.\n- `selection.rs`, `interact.rs` and `model.rs` were over 400 lines before this PR. This PR adds one or two lines to each and does not split them.\n\nChangelog: The viewport stays fast with chains in an operation's geometry selection: the selection's chains and pocket region are computed once when the selection or the model changes, not on each frame.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2235\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
